<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordoño II of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 924</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ordoño II was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias">Alfonso III of Asturias</a> who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> when his father's realm was divided in 910. On the death of his brother García I in 914 he also became king of León, made the city of León his royal seat and so gave the kingdom its name. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a> with mixed success and died in 924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordono-ii-of-leon.jpg" alt="Ordoño II of León" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ordono_II_of_Le%C3%B3n_Leon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
